summary is: {{ Beverly is a 24 year old female with a history of type 2 diabetes mellitus and hypertension. She presented for her yearly exam. She had not been seen in a year. She began working in a bakery that summer and found herself snacking a lot during shifts and eating a lot more desserts than she normally would. Her blood sugars were up and down because of diet, she attributed, because she was taking her medication as prescribed. She had not missed anything else. The only thing that was different was her diet, pretty much. Because of the new job and all that. She found it really challenging to resist the temptation. She had no willpower like me? (laughs)
She had high blood pressure, hypertension. How were her blood sugars? Had she been checking them? She said her blood pressure's been good. Um, despite her, um, her diabetes levels being up and down. So, that's been good. She had no concerns about hurting herself or anything like that. She was getting a full eight hours of sleep. No swelling in her neck. No swelling in her legs. No swelling in her belly. She had no pain. She had no fevers. She had no cough. She had no shortness of breath. She had no chest pain. She had no abdominal pain. She had no nausea. She had no vomiting. She had no diarrhea. She had no constipation. She had no headaches. She had no dizziness. She had no falls. She had no chest pain. She had no palpitations. She had no skin rashes. She had no joint pains. She had no muscle pains. She had no back pains. She had no pelvic pains. She had no penile or testicular pains. She had no rectal bleeding. She had no penile discharge. She had no urinary retention. She had no urinary frequency. She had no hematuria. She had no dysuria. She had no flank pain. She had no testicular pain. She had no penile pain. She had no breast pain. She had no testicular pain. She had no penile discharge. She had no vaginal }}<|eot_id|>
