summary is: {{ Dax is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease who presents with left elbow pain. Dax works as a data entry clerk at a local hospital. She sits at a desk all day typing on a keyboard. She states that she repetitively flexes her left elbow to the extent of 90 degrees, specifically at the keyboard and mouse. She states that after work, it is difficult for her to extend and flex her left elbow. She reports left elbow pain, swelling, and stiffness. She denies any numbness, tingling, or weakness in her left arm. She denies any fever, chills, chest pain, shortness of breath, abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting. She endorses nasal congestion from allergies.
Dax is right-hand dominant. She can still write but has difficulty typing. She has not had any recent seizures. She is currently taking keppra 500 mg twice daily for epilepsy. She has been in therapy for depression and has not wanted to take any medication since she is already on keppra. She has been experiencing some stressors in her life. She has had an episode of gastritis a year ago that required an upper endoscopy, which showed peptic ulcer disease. She has been taking protonix 40 mg once daily before meals and has not had any further issues with her peptic ulcer disease.
On physical examination, she has vital signs within normal limits. She has erythema and edema of her left elbow. She has pain to palpation of the olecranon. She is warm to palpation. She has some weakness in her left arm. She can barely flex her left elbow. She has a palpable right radial pulse. She has a normal left radial pulse. She has no other focal neurological deficits.
Her left elbow x-ray is shown below in Figure. Her endoscopy is shown below in Figure.
Based on the information, Dax has olecranon bursitis from repetitive trauma, meloxicam 15 mg once daily, ice the area, and a pillow for her elbow. She is doing well with her epilepsy and will continue keppra 500 mg twice daily. She is doing well with her depression and will start lexapro 10 mg once daily. She will continue protonix 40 mg once daily before meals for her peptic ulcer disease. }}<|eot_id|>
