lp strengthen his his lower extremities also and I want him to come back to me within you know a week to ten days following his first couple physical therapy appointments so I can monitor how he's doing I see no reason for an x-ray at this point but if this continues we're gon na you know if he's still having pain ten days in significant pain without change modification of his activity then we may have to look at more aggressive treatment plans how does that sound for him? Sounds good. Hey did you happen to catch that pittsburgh pang one hockey game last night? No i i was watching the track meet. My gosh the the pang ones are on fire you know they beat up on new york seven to two i mean the hockey's just an amazing sport i i just do you guy do a lot of hockey down there in town here? Used to when i lived in detroit. Oh. No yeah detroit is a hockey town yeah the red wings okay well I'm gon na go ahead and I'll send my nurse in and go ahead and get him discharged and like I said I'd like to see him back here in seven to ten days after that first physical therapy appointment I've got a great phenomenal office staff you just call in once that gets scheduled they will get you in to that next available appointment so take care and I will talk to you later. }}<|eot_id|>
