summary is: {{ A seventy seven year old male with past medical history significant for hypertension, stage three chronic kidney disease and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease presents to the hospital for follow up after an acute on chronic chf exacerbation. The patient had been recently discharged home with a plan to continue on bumex two milligrams one daily, cozaar a hundred milligrams daily and norvasc five milligrams once daily. On hospital day two, the patient was found to have a blood pressure of two hundred over ninety on the telemetry monitor. The patient stated that he had been watching his diet as instructed but had noticed that his ankles were swelling. He stated that he had been having shortness of breath and had to call nine one one. When the paramedics arrived, they placed him on a special mask to breathe. On arrival to the er, his blood pressure was two hundred over ninety. The patient was notified that he was in the hospital for heart failure. The patient stated that he had been trying to watch his diet but had some slips. He stated that he was a big cheese man and loved him some football and that he and his friends would go to parties on the weekends. He stated that he just could not help it that he really liked pizza and loved chicken wings and that he would eat them when he was with his friends. He stated that he knew he should not eat them but that they were good and that he wanted to eat them. The patient stated that he had been feeling good until the shortness of breath and that he was told he had a heart problem. The patient was told that he had a heart failure exacerbation and was admitted to the hospital. The patient stated that he did not want to go back to the hospital and that he wanted to take care of himself. The patient was told that he needed to watch his diet and take his medications as instructed. He was also told to buy a blood pressure cuff at home. The patient stated that he finally did what the doctor said and ordered one and it came last week. He stated that he checks it about every other day and that his blood pressure has been really good. He stated that he has not had any shortness of breath or problems sleeping and that he does not have any chest pain. The patient was told that he needed to rest every now and then as well. On physical exam, the patient was afebrile with a blood pressure of one twenty eight over seventy two. His vital signs were stable. His heart rate was nice at like seventy nine. His respiratory rate was twenty six probably because he was talking to the doctor. His o2 sat was ninety nine percent. On neck exam, there was no jugular venous distention. On heart exam, he appreciated a two out of six systolic ejection murmur which was stable. On lungs, they were clear bilaterally. On lower extremities, they showed a trace of edema. The patient was told that this would be helped with the water pills that he was taking. The patient was told that he would need to continue on bumex two milligrams one daily and cozaar a hundred milligrams daily. He was also told to continue to watch his diet. The patient was told that he would need to get labs to make sure that he tolerated this regimen. }}<|eot_id|>
